//
// Phase F study harness: the host-only test suite, behind the one entry point.
//
// This is doc 09 work item 5 -- "define how it is installed, discovered and
// invoked from CMake/lit -- a single .lit wrapper so `ninja check-...` remains
// the one entry point". lit discovers *.lit by glob, so this file needs no
// registration; the suite it runs discovers test_*.py by glob for the same
// reason.
//
// No NPU, no XRT, no compilation and no framework. The study tier's schema,
// results I/O, smoke gate, manifest, iron adapter and ladder shape override are
// all pure host logic, so they gate here rather than waiting for a device.
// pytest is not installed in the sandbox venv and installing it while a gate or
// a measurement run is live is the hazard doc 09 records, so these modules run
// as plain scripts -- written to be collectible by pytest unchanged if it ever
// lands, but depending on none of it. Same choice, and the same reasoning, as
// run_block_cache_tests.lit.
//
// THE COUNT IS PINNED ON PURPOSE. Discovery alone cannot catch a test that
// stops being *defined*: delete a test function and a globbing runner happily
// reports a smaller suite passing. Convention rule 11 exists because iron's
// pytest.ini collected none of its own study/test_*.py by directory, and that
// hid real bugs. So the module count and the test count are both matched
// exactly, and a suite that quietly shrinks fails here instead of passing.
//
// Update the numbers below when you add tests. That edit is the point, not
// friction to route around with a looser pattern.
//
// RUN: python3 %S/study/run_host_tests.py | FileCheck %s
// CHECK: study host tests: 196/196 passed in 15 modules
